CAT = ("laundry-tabs", "Laundry tab questions", "The questions people ask most about laundry tabs, answered for Just 7.")
P = "†"
QA = [
("How are laundry detergent tabs made?", "Dry ingredients are blended and pressed into tablets under pressure. Just 7 adds no water to ship; the only water is the little that comes in with the cleaners."),
("How do laundry tabs work?", "In water, Just 7's citric acid and washing soda fizz and the cellulose swells, breaking the tab apart. Then the cleaners and water softeners get to work, like a liquid would."),
("What do laundry tabs do?", "They clean clothes, the same job as liquid or powder detergent, in a dry pre-measured tab."),
("Why did Just 7 switch from sheets to tabs?", "We first planned a laundry sheet. A pressed tab let us drop the film entirely, no PVA and no film of any kind, and still keep the list to seven ingredients."),
("Is the Just 7 formula different from the sheet you showed before?", "Yes. The tab uses sodium carbonate, citric acid, sodium citrate, microcrystalline cellulose, lauryl glucoside, decyl glucoside and water. The film and glycerin are gone. [Ingredients](/pages/ingredients/)."),
("Why is the website still just7sheets.com?", "That's the address we started with, and it still gets you to Just 7. The product is Just 7 Laundry Tabs."),
("I pre-ordered the sheets. What happens now?", "A pre-order is just your email, and nothing has been charged. You'll hear about Just 7 Laundry Tabs first, and you can unsubscribe anytime."),
("Are laundry tabs safe?", "We don't make safety claims. Use as directed and store any detergent sealed and away from kids and pets."),
("Are laundry tabs toxic?", "\"Toxic\" depends on dose and exposure, and any detergent can harm if eaten. Store tabs out of reach and read the full ingredient list."),
("Are laundry tabs bad for you?", "We don't make health claims. You can check all seven of our ingredients on our [ingredients page](/pages/ingredients/)."),
("Are laundry tabs bad for your washer?", "Used as directed, no. Put the tab in the drum, not the dispenser, and don't overload."),
("Do laundry tabs dissolve completely?", "Just 7 is designed to break up fully in the wash, with a light fizz to help.† Overloading and very cold, short cycles are the usual culprits when bits remain."),
("Do I put the tab in the drum or the drawer?", "The drum. Tab in first, clothes on top. Not the detergent drawer."),
("Why does the tab fizz?", "Citric acid and washing soda react in water. The light fizz helps the tab break up, even in cold water.†"),
("Can I unwrap a Just 7 tab?", "There's nothing to unwrap. Each tab is pressed, not wrapped, so there's no film or PVA."),
("How big is a Just 7 tab?", "About 30 mm (1.2 in) across and 4 g.†"),
("Can I cut a tab in half for a small load?", "We don't recommend it. One tab is the dose for small and regular loads; use two for large or messy ones."),
("Do laundry tabs contain plastic?", "Some tabs and most pods use a PVA film. Just 7 tabs have no film at all.†"),
("Do laundry tabs have microplastics?", "We don't add any plastic to Just 7: no film, no PVA. We'll back the finished tab up with test data.†"),
("Where are laundry detergent tabs made?", "It varies by brand. We'll state where Just 7 is made on the pouch before launch."),
("Where can I buy laundry tabs?", "Just 7 is on just7sheets.com. Pre-order now. Coming soon."),
("Do laundry tabs stick together or crumble?", "They can in humid air. Keep the pouch sealed and handle tabs with dry hands."),
("Do laundry tabs work for heavily soiled clothes?", "Use two tabs and pretreat. For heavy protein stains, Just 9 is planned."),
("Do laundry tabs need fabric softener?", "No. Softener is optional."),
("Are laundry tabs good for towels?", "Yes. Use one tab, skip softener and dry fully."),
("Are laundry tabs good for whites?", "Yes for everyday whites. Add oxygen bleach for tough stains."),
("Can laundry tabs cause skin irritation?", "Any detergent can bother some people. Just 7 skips fragrance and dyes, and an extra rinse helps if you're sensitive."),
("How long do laundry tabs last once opened?", "Many months if the pouch stays sealed and dry between uses."),
("Can laundry tabs get wet before use?", "Avoid it. Water starts the fizz, and damp tabs can crumble."),
("Can I use a laundry tab that got damp?", "Yes, use it in the next wash."),
("How many tabs for a king comforter?", "Two tabs, on a bulky cycle with an extra rinse."),
("How many tabs for a load of towels?", "One tab for a regular load of towels, two for a full drum."),
("How many loads does a pouch do?", "Up to 60: one tab per small or regular load, two for large.†"),
("Are laundry tabs good value?", "Compare per load: Just 7 is $15 for 60 tabs with subscribe and save, about $0.25 a regular load.†"),
("Do laundry tabs smell?", "Scented ones do; Just 7 has no smell at all."),
("Are laundry tabs good for the environment?", "Dry formats cut jug waste and shipping weight. Wrappers and packaging matter too, which is why Just 7 has no film. [Honest look](/blogs/planet/are-laundry-detergent-sheets-really-better-for-the-planet/)."),
("Do laundry tabs work as well as liquid detergent on everyday dirt?", "We're running a side-by-side test before making any claim for Just 7.†"),
("How do I know laundry tabs are working?", "Clothes come out clean and smell like nothing. If a smell remains, rewash with two tabs."),
("Can I use laundry tabs for delicates?", "Yes. One tab, cold water, delicate cycle, or dissolve it first and hand-wash."),
("Can I travel with laundry tabs?", "Yes. They're dry, so they're not limited like liquids. Check current airline and TSA rules before you fly."),
("What's the best laundry tab?", "The one whose label you're happy with. Compare ingredients, wrappers and cost per load. Just 7 is built for a short label."),
("Can laundry tabs damage clothes?", "Used as directed, Just 7 is a normal laundry detergent with no bleach. Follow care labels."),
]
